# Gemini CLI - Unmute Project Context

This file provides context and instructions for Gemini CLI when working on the Unmute project.

## Project Overview
Unmute is a real-time system that allows text-based Large Language Models (LLMs) to listen and speak. It uses Kyutai's Speech-to-Text (STT) and Text-to-Speech (TTS) models to bridge the gap between voice and text.

### Key Technologies
- **Backend:** Python 3.12 (FastAPI), `fastrtc`, `websockets`, `pydantic`.
- **Frontend:** Next.js (React), Tailwind CSS, `pnpm`.
- **Models:** Kyutai STT/TTS, VLLM (for local LLM hosting), MCP (Model Context Protocol).
- **Orchestration:** Docker Compose, Traefik (reverse proxy), Prometheus/Grafana (monitoring).

## Architecture
```mermaid
graph LR
    UB[User browser]
    UB --> B(Backend)
    UB --> F(Frontend)
    B --> STT(Speech-to-text)
    B --> LLM_Proxy(LLM Proxy)
    LLM_Proxy --> LLM(VLLM/OpenAI/Ollama)
    B --> TTS(Text-to-speech)
```
- **Backend (`unmute/main_websocket.py`):** Handles real-time WebSocket connections using a protocol based on the OpenAI Realtime API (ORA).
- **UnmuteHandler (`unmute/unmute_handler.py`):** The core logic that coordinates STT, LLM Proxy, and TTS. Manages conversation state, VAD interruptions, and turn transitions.
- **LLM Proxy (`unmute/llm_proxy/`):** An intermediate service that adds tool calling (via MCP) and "thinking mode" to standard LLM providers. It implements true streaming for the final response even after multiple tool-calling rounds, ensuring minimal Time To First Token (TTFT).
- **Frontend (`frontend/`):** A Next.js application providing the user interface and audio processing in the browser.

## UI & UX Mandates (Design Guidelines)
- **Header:** The `UnmuteHeader` must be fixed at the **top-left** of the interface.
- **Audio Visualizers:** The two circular visualizers must be **centered and stacked** (superimposed).
  - The **User circle (White)** must always be **on top** (higher z-index) of the **Assistant circle (Green)**.
  - The User circle must have a radius exactly **20px larger** than the Assistant circle.
- **Media Sidebar:** 
  - All detected links and images from the LLM responses must be grouped in a `MediaSidebar` at the **top-right**.
  - The sidebar must be **collapsible** (click on title) but must **auto-expand** whenever a new item is added.
  - Height must be limited (`max-h-[60vh]`) to avoid UI overlap.

## Core Architectural Rules
- **TTS Normalization & Filtering:** 
  - All URLs (regex matched) must be **filtered out** from the text stream sent to the TTS engine.
  - Use `normalize_text_for_tts` in `unmute/unmute_handler.py` to convert symbols (€, $, %), units (m/s, km/h), and ordinals (1er, 16e) into spoken text.
- **Tool Management & Security:**
  - All tools must be filtered against names in `/app/mcp-tools-excluded.json`.
  - Tool name matching must be **robust**: handle names with/without underscores and ignore case.
  - **Parallel Execution**: Tools within the same round must be executed in parallel using `asyncio.gather` in the proxy.
- **Instant Acknowledgement**: The LLM Proxy must inject an "eager acknowledgement" phrase (e.g., "Un instant, je vérifie...") immediately when a tool call is detected in the stream, to avoid user-perceived silence.
- **History Management**: 
  - The `reset_recent_interactions` tool must truncate **X+1** interactions to include the reset request itself.
  - History reset events (`unmute.reset_history`) must be synced between the proxy and the backend.
- **Thinking Mode:** Supported for both OpenAI and Ollama (via the `think` parameter). Default value read from `THINKING_MODE_DEFAULT`.
- **Google Workspace Tool**: `get_next_calendar_events` must aggregate events from the primary calendar and the shared calendar defined by `SHARED_CALENDAR_ID`.

## Development Guidelines

### Prerequisites
- **Python:** 3.12 (managed with `uv`).
- **Node.js:** `pnpm` for frontend.
- **Hardware:** NVIDIA GPU with 16GB+ VRAM and NVIDIA Container Toolkit.

### Building and Running
- **Full Stack (Docker):** `docker compose up --build`
- **Backend (Dev Mode):** `uv run fastapi dev unmute/main_websocket.py`
- **Frontend (Dev Mode):** `cd frontend && pnpm dev`
- **LLM Proxy (Dev Mode):** `uv run uvicorn unmute.llm_proxy.main:app --reload --port 8081`

### Tool Usage in this Repository
- **`uv`:** Always use `uv run` or `uv pip` for Python-related tasks.
- **`pnpm`:** Always use `pnpm` for frontend tasks.
- **`git`:** Do not commit `voices.yaml`, `.env`, or `mcp-servers.json` if they contain secrets.
